┌─────────────────────────────── Game Concept ────────────────────────────────┐
│ Coldstore                                                                   │
│ A decommissioned harbor cold-store: a three-room refrigerated warehouse     │
│ abandoned when the cannery folded, now picked over by scavengers who rarely │
│ all walk back out. You enter through the gutting floor, and the only way    │
│ home is the loading dock on the far side of the freezer.                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  Regions: The Coldstore
  Items: 11 created
  Quests: 6  |  NPCs: 5
  Style: Tight 32x32px pixel art on a strict integer grid — every sprite, tile,
and prop authored at 32x32 native and rendered at integer scale only (3x/4x, 
nearest-neighbor, no bilinear, no sub-pixel camera). Characters occupy a 16w x 
28h silhouette within their 32x32 cell, read-first (recognizable in one 
flickering frame) with hunched, cold-braced posture. Environment is 
orthographic top-down-3/4 (2:1 dimetric feel faked in flat tiles) so roller 
doors, gutting tables, and shelving read as depth without true perspective. 
Hard 1px outlines are selective, not universal: full dark outline (#1a1418) 
only where a sprite meets lit floor; outlines DROP to interior shading where a 
sprite sits in shadow, so figures visually dissolve into the dark exactly like 
the Listener does. Dithering is the signature technique — 2x2 and 4x4 Bayer 
checker dithers carry every shadow gradient and every frost-to-rust transition;
never use smooth anti-aliased ramps, the grain IS the mood. Palette is 
hard-capped: max 6 hues + 4 neutral values per sprite. Frost rime is painted as
1-2px stippled highlight clusters on top edges of steel; rust is a dithered 
mid-brown bleed pooling at bottom edges and weld seams. Loot containers use a 
shared 32x32 silhouette language with tier-coded lid trim (see palette) so 
players read value at a glance. Extraction zone is a 2x2 tile stencil of amber 
hazard-chevrons that pulses. UI is diegetic-minimal: a bottom rig-slot strip 
(4-6 slots, 24x24 item icons), a 3-segment thin outline map of the loop, and an
8-second extract ring drawn as a depleting 32px arc.
┌───────────────────────────────── QA Report ─────────────────────────────────┐
│ Score: 6/10                                                                 │
│ Coldstore is an exceptionally cohesive and atmospheric design — the         │
│ three-room extraction loop, sound-hunting Listener, noise/greed tension,    │
│ and permadeath re-seeding all reinforce each other, and the NPC/item/lore   │
│ layer is tight and evocative. However, it is not yet playable as specified. │
│ Two blockers stop progression: (1) the referenced loot table                │
│ 'loot_coldstore_weighted' is undefined and containers have no drop mapping, │
│ and (2) collect objectives mix container-entity IDs with item IDs (notably  │
│ cs_frozen_stock_tin is never actually spawnable), making core quests        │
│ uncompletable. Major gaps compound this: stat_system and combat_system are  │
│ both null despite items, a 120-HP boss kill, level gates (2/3), and rig     │
│ slot mechanics all depending on them; and three quests are anchored to      │
│ rooms their givers can never reach. Fix the loot/data integrity, define the │
│ missing stat/combat systems and rig slot count, and reconcile quest-giver   │
│ locations, then re-run QA against an actual build. Strong foundation,       │
│ blocked on implementation-level definitions.                                │
│ Issues: 10  |  Playable: No                                                 │
